{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a mild, visible-light photoredox catalytic method for the direct N-(het)arylation of lactams. Using 4CzIPN as an organic photocatalyst and pyridinium-based nitrogen radical precursors, the authors achieved the regioselective addition of N-centered lactam radicals to various arenes and heteroarenes. The method is compatible with aqueous media and was successfully scaled up using continuous flow reactors.",
